// feed_image_overlay.proto — THE IMAGE OVERLAY: one image drawn large over
// the feed's rows, opened by a click on an image anywhere -- a thumbnail in
// the Emacs input window, a prompt bubble's image, a held card's image, a
// tool card's image -- and closed by a click on the overlay or Escape.
//
//   ┌ feed ─────────────────────────────────────────┐
//   │ ┌ overlay ──────────────────────────────────┐ │   FeedImageOverlay.open
//   │ │                                           │ │
//   │ │              [ the image ]                │ │   FeedImageOverlayOpen.image
//   │ │                                           │ │
//   │ └───────────────────────────────────────────┘ │
//   └───────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//
// The overlay sits over the part of the feed the rows stream into, just shy
// of its width and height, so the rows stay visible around its edge: it is
// not a full-window viewer.
//
// THE DAEMON HOLDS IT, PER WORKSPACE. A click in Emacs and a click in the
// webapp are two producers of one state, so the state lives where both can
// reach it: the daemon keeps each workspace's overlay and pushes it on that
// workspace's ROOT feed watch (WatchFeedResponse.image_overlay). It survives
// switching away from the workspace and back, and a page that opens late is
// told what is open the moment its watch is accepted.

